    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras head into today\u2019s slate with a condensed active roster due to a lack of volume, making our three available starters pivotal for maintaining offensive production. **Trea Turner** (66.39) remains our premier option; while Christian Scott presents a respectable 3.94 xERA, **Trea Turner**\u2019s elite speed and anticipated leadoff spot mitigate the threat of the right-handed matchup. Similarly, **Kyle Schwarber** (63.04) carries a strong score despite the same rain risk, anchored by a robust 0.377 xwOBA that justifies the start. **Carson Benge** (54.68) sits firmly in the marginal tier, but he earns his spot against Aaron Nola by capitalizing on a platoon edge that provides a +7% boost to his base projection, helping him bridge the gap where a higher-upside bat might otherwise be required.\n\nThe bench situation is stark today, with key pillars like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Christian Yelich** all sidelined by scheduled team off-days. Consequently, there were no competitive bench decisions to be made; the system defaulted to the only three active bats available. The primary concern for the squad remains the 31% rain risk at the stadium, which threatens to disrupt the rhythm for **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Carson Benge**. With the rest of our depth\u2014including **Caleb Durbin**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**\u2014entirely dormant, we are heavily reliant on these three to capture the stolen bases and counting stats necessary to keep pace in this 5x5 format.",
